* Developed with AI assistance from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) -- 17 Nov 2026
* oorexx.pfx -- ooRexx definition for the prefix-macro framework
* (phase B).  Format as in rexx.pfx; shares src\pfxrexx.src with REXX.
* Source: Open Object Rexx Reference, ooRexx 5.2.0 (rexxref, edition
* 2026.04.18): LOOP (2.14), DO/LOOP OVER and WITH (2.4), SELECT CASE
* (2.27), directives (chapter 3), line comments and the - continuation
* (1.10).  See BIBLIOGRAPHY.md.
*
* The macro is PFXOOREXX; the XEDIT file name is truncated to the CMS
* limit of 8 characters, PFXOOREX XEDIT.
§lang       ooRexx
§macro      PFXOOREXX
*
* Keyword case: the templates as written (ASIS); the user may ask for
* LOWER or UPPER (option <macro>_CASE / GLOBALV PFX_CASE).
§case       asis
§source     rexx
§unit       DO=3 IF=3 label=3 SELECT=1 WHEN=2
*
* Mask for the body lines the macro adds, as for REXX.
§mask       40:/* 70:*/ op:&placeholder
*
* Look-back: which lines don't govern indentation.  ooRexx adds the
* line comment -- and the continuation character -.
§comment    /* */
§linecomment --
§continue   trailing , -
§blank      skip
§label      colon label
*
* Indentation after the governing line's keyword: LOOP opens a block
* as DO does.
§opens      DO=DO LOOP=DO ELSE=IF IF=IF SELECT=SELECT WHEN=WHEN OTHERWISE=WHEN
§nested     WHEN OTHERWISE
§dedent     WHEN=WHEN
*
* After a line starting with END (at the body's column), the insert
* aligns with the line the END closes (his original intent).
§closes     END
*
* ---- commands ----
§cmd        DO          §min 2  §desc Insert DO block
§var        -           §first do                        §cursor body
§var        FOREVER 1   §first do forever                §cursor body
§var        UNTIL 1     §first do until &placeholder     §cursor 9
§var        WHILE 1     §first do while &placeholder     §cursor 9
§var        OVER 1      §first do &placeholder over &placeholder §cursor 3
§var        WITH 2      §first do with index &placeholder item &placeholder over &placeholder §cursor 14
§var        *           §first do %op                    §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end
*
§cmd        LOOP        §min 3  §desc Insert LOOP block; a plain LOOP repeats forever
§var        -           §first loop                      §cursor body
§var        UNTIL 1     §first loop until &placeholder   §cursor 11
§var        WHILE 1     §first loop while &placeholder   §cursor 11
§var        OVER 1      §first loop &placeholder over &placeholder §cursor 5
§var        WITH 2      §first loop with index &placeholder item &placeholder over &placeholder §cursor 16
§var        *           §first loop %op                  §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end
*
§cmd        IF          §min 2  §desc Insert IF
§first      if &placeholder then do                       §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end
§row        text=else do
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end
*
§cmd        SELECT      §min 3  §desc Insert SELECT block; SELECT CASE selects by the value of an expression
§var        -           §first select
§var        CASE 1      §first select case &placeholder  §cursor 12
§row        indent=SELECT text=when &placeholder then do  §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end
§row        indent=SELECT text=otherwise do
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end
§row        indent=SELECT text=end
*
§cmd        WHEN        §min 3  §desc Insert WHEN clause
§first      when &placeholder then do                     §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end
*
§cmd        OTHERWISE   §min 4  §desc Insert OTHERWISE clause
§first      otherwise do                                  §cursor body
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end
*
§cmd        ITERATE     §min 4  §desc Insert ITERATE; the cursor follows the keyword, for an optional loop name
§first      iterate                                       §cursor 8
*
§cmd        LEAVE       §min 3  §desc Insert LEAVE; the cursor follows the keyword, for an optional loop name
§first      leave                                         §cursor 6
*
* ---- directives: the body starts in column 1 ----
§cmd        CLASS       §min 3  §desc Insert ::CLASS directive
§first      ::class &placeholder                          §cursor 8
*
§cmd        METHOD      §min 3  §desc Insert ::METHOD directive and body
§first      ::method &placeholder                         §cursor 9
§row        pend=RIC
*
§cmd        ROUTINE     §min 3  §desc Insert ::ROUTINE directive and body
§first      ::routine &placeholder                        §cursor 10
§row        pend=RIC
*
§cmd        RESOURCE    §min 3  §desc Insert ::RESOURCE directive and its ::END
§first      ::resource &placeholder                       §cursor 11
§row        text=::END
*
* Engine built-ins this language uses (no template): pending and case
* commands. Synonyms are the names the setup registers.
§builtin    .. CLINE RI RIC CLC CUC
§synonym    LOC=CLC UPC=CUC
